Back in 2002 when i first played half - life game, i was shocked. It was first game that truly impressed me. Dynamic and unpredictable storyline with first npc's that weren't just some guys that gave you some tasks and information, but they were really interesting characters. And they could interact with player. That was awesome when i was child. Now i wanted to replay first half - life. But if i can still play half - life 2, graphic in first game is..... well, let's admit: it is really painful to play that game by now:)
And we have Black Mesa. It's pity they hadn't finished Zen yet, but i can wait. At least it is gonna be done, unlike half - life 3.(  I can say that even if you played first half - life, you still should buy it, because it is complete overhaul. They didn't just implroved graphic, they added many moments that weren't in original game. And if you are new to half - life series, than it's just important for you to play one of the most iconic FPS game in the gaming history!
This game is so detailed and has so much advantages such as
*Strong storyline;
*Really good FPS side and variety of weapons;
*One of the best characters -  G-man;
*Really good cinematic scenes;
*Gorgeous OST (they made new soundtrack for Black Mesa. For me it is better than in original game;
And  many others. I can only say that one of the few cons of the game was Freeman. It is just walking machine without any emotion or voice. It is strange that he is one the best characters in the history of computer games. And some moments were too long (they could cut it in some places). And, i think, game was just too hard for me. Is it just me or game, i don't really know.
Should you own the game? Well, why haven't you already done that?) Go and enjoy it right now. My score to game is 90 out of 100.

